 THE SPOTIFY VERIFICATION — assumption disproved
 -----------------------------------------------
2026-07-30 08:10:00 — [INFO] Credentials supplied by the author. Ran the real check.
2026-07-30 08:11:00 — [INFO] Authentication succeeded: Client Credentials token OK
2026-07-30 08:12:00 — [CRITICAL] The assumed response shape was WRONG.
                                 GET /v1/search?type=artist returns a SIMPLIFIED
                                 object: external_urls, href, id, images, name,
                                 type, uri. No followers, popularity or genres.
2026-07-30 08:13:00 — [CRITICAL] GET /v1/artists/{id} returns 200 with the SAME
                                 keys — the metrics are absent there too
2026-07-30 08:13:30 — [CRITICAL] GET /v1/artists?ids=   -> 403 Forbidden
                                 GET /v1/artists/{id}/top-tracks -> 403 Forbidden
                                 GET /v1/artists/{id}/albums     -> 200
2026-07-30 08:14:00 — [INFO] Conclusion: Spotify no longer exposes metrics to newly
                             registered applications. Not a project defect, not the
                             author's mistake — a platform restriction.
2026-07-30 08:14:30 — [WARNING] This is exactly why the module was flagged unverified
                                in session 05. tests/test_spotify.py had been written
                                against the documented shape, passed green, and was
                                asserting something false. A test passing on a wrong
                                assumption is worse than no test: it manufactures
                                confidence.
2026-07-30 08:15:00 — [FIXED]   Tests rewritten against the OBSERVED shape, including
                                one that asserts the metric fields are absent — if
                                Spotify ever restores them, it fails and tells us.

