 WHAT WAS BUILT
 --------------
2026-07-30 11:15:00 — [INFO] analytics/popularity.py — index = mean(top-10 rank)/10,000
2026-07-30 11:16:00 — [INFO] Mean, not maximum, and the reason is documented: one viral
                             hit would spike the maximum and misdescribe an artist whose
                             remaining catalogue is barely played
2026-07-30 11:17:00 — [INFO] Lives in analytics/, not api/: it is a derived metric, not
                             something a source handed us
2026-07-30 11:18:00 — [INFO] Labelled as CALCULATED everywhere it appears — report, web,
                             README. It is not a platform metric and not a play count,
                             and presenting it as either would misinform.
2026-07-30 11:22:00 — [INFO] Tracks are now fetched during PERCEIVE rather than ACT: the
                             index derives from them, so it has to be part of the
                             snapshot that gets stored. Otherwise popularity could never
                             become a time series.
2026-07-30 11:24:00 — [INFO] The daily collector computes it too — without that the
                             history would only ever accumulate followers
2026-07-30 11:28:00 — [INFO] Metrics no source publishes are now REMOVED from the report
